        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>Element Name</td><td>Type</td><td>Semantics</td></tr><tr><td>Header</td><td>complexType: MessageHeaderType Refer to 8.3.3</td><td>Contains general information, used for all messages.</td></tr><tr><td>EVProcessing</td><td>simpleType: processingType enumeration refer to Annex A for the type definition</td><td>Parameter indicating that the EV is Finished with the PowerDelivery and will send a different Message next. If set to ongoing, it indicates that the EVCC needs more time to calculate the EVPowerProfile.</td></tr><tr><td>ChargeProgress</td><td>simpleType: chargeProgressType enumeration refer to Annex A for the type definition</td><td>This message element is used to request the EVSE to fulfill all conditions that the energy transfer can start as soon as the EV onboard system begins to retrieve energy without any further action to be taken (i.e. the EVSE is requested to close its contactors successfully). If ChargeProgress is equal to &quot;Start&quot; the EVSE is requested to prepare the energy flow for an immediate start. If ChargeProgress is equal to &quot;Stop&quot; the EVSE is requested to stop the energy flow. If ChargeProgress is equal to &quot;ScheduleRenegotiation&quot; the energy flow is neither stopped nor started, instead the schedule renegotiation mechanisms defined in this document apply. If ChargeProgress is equal to &quot;Standby&quot;, the EVSE is notified that EV wants to enter a standby period, and if accepted by EVSE, EVSE shall stop the energy flow. If ChargeProgress is equal to &quot;Pause&quot;, the EVSE is notified that EV wants to enter a pause period, and if accepted by EVSE, EVSE shall stop the energy flow and shutdown the communication to be resumed at a later time (as indicated by the EVPowerProfile in scheduled control mode).</td></tr></table>",
